Third-party code
================

Sagitta is a fork of quiver (https://github.com/varkor/quiver), by varkor and
its contributors, reworked into a keyboard-driven desktop editor. It bundles
KaTeX 0.16.25 (src/katex.js, katex.css, and fonts/), with only the woff2
fonts kept. Both are
MIT-licensed, and their notices follow. Sagitta as a whole, including its
changes to quiver's code, is under the GPL above; KaTeX's files, taken on
their own, remain under KaTeX's license.

quiver credits, among others, S. C. Steenkamp (aesthetic rendering of arrows),
AndréC (the TikZ style for curves of a fixed height), Andrew Stacey (the TikZ
style for shortened curves), Paolo Brasolin (offline support), and Carl
Davidson (loop rendering).


